{
  "$comment": "Ask the HQ golden set (spec section 9). 18 benchmark questions, 14 new, 6 perspective questions (spec section 13; q37 and q38 have no written view and must be refused) 3 CV refresh questions (q39 to q41, CV of 2026-10-13) 1 observability question (q42, \"How I run AI in production\", 2026-10-14) 2 Data and ML questions (q43 and q44, owner request 2026-10-14) and 3 questions about how this site was built (q45 to q47, content/ask/site-build.json, owner request 2026-10-15). 12 owner-request questions (q48 to q59, 2026-10-15): capabilities (EN, ID), lead intent with and without a matching project (EN, ID), three lifestyle and two policy questions from his written perspectives, and a partisan politics refusal. 4 nickname questions (q60 to q63, owner request 2026-10-16): ShinyQ is his nickname, so these ask who it is and what he does, in EN and ID. 1 MII Cowork question (q64, owner request 2026-10-16). 1 Clearbox question (q65, owner request 2026-10-16). 1 Sewise Fashion Labs question (q66, owner request 2026-10-16). 1 Google certification question (q75, owner request 2026-10-18). 3 follow-up questions (q72 to q74, multi-turn memory, owner decision 2026-10-17): `history` lists the earlier questions, which the eval asks first and whose model answers join the history, as signed turns do in production. `facts` must exist in the knowledge pack (drift check) and in the retrieved context (retrieval check). Values from the weekly live facts (content/generated/dynamic-facts.json) are written as {{facts.<path>}} placeholders, never literals (src/ask/golden-facts.ts). `expect` scores the real-model answer in the nightly eval (scripts/ask-eval.ts). 1 B1 Engine Room question (q76, 2026-10-17; the plan said q72, then q75, both taken on main). Update this file in the same PR as content changes that move these facts.",
  "passThreshold": 73,
